Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Stained Glass OS -- the touch keyboard (sg-touchkbd, TabTip.exe). It starts
; at sign-in in the background (the machine's Run key, as Windows' touch
; keyboard service does) and stays only on a computer with a touch screen or a
; pen (or with "Show touch keyboard button" on): a button in the notification
; area, and the keyboard showing itself when a text field is touched with no
; hardware keyboard attached. TabTip.exe through App Paths is how programs
; show it themselves.
;
; The path is the package's install location reached through Z:. If Z: is ever
; removed from the prefix for isolation, this must move with it.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run]
"TouchKeyboard"="Z:\\usr\\libexec\\stained-glass\\shell\\sg-touchkbd64.exe /background"

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\App Paths\TabTip.exe]
@="Z:\\usr\\libexec\\stained-glass\\shell\\sg-touchkbd64.exe"
